[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_traveller"
text = "# DRAFT
# The traveller beside the porter on the carter's wagon, night 0. The carter has pulled in; as the cart with the covered body comes close the traveller breaks off whatever he was saying (traveller_road.tres is that talk) and turns to it.
# If the porter told him he's the abbey's porter (n0_road_porter), he says your abbey; if not, the carter has told him.
== start
Traveller: Whoa. Look at that.
(The cart creaks by close enough to touch. Something long lies under sacking on its bed.)
Traveller: That's a man under the sacking, brother.
* God rest him. Who was he? -> who
* What happened to him? -> what
* (Cross yourself, and pray for him.) -> pray

== who
Traveller: Nobody knows. Nobody ever knows them. A pilgrim's badge on his hat, and his purse gone.
-> third

== what
Traveller: Found in the ditch by the white chapel, the carter says. Not a mark on him that anyone will talk about.
-> third

== pray
(You say the words for the dead under your breath. The traveller watches you do it.)
Traveller: Say one for yourself while you're at it.
-> third

== third
-> third_porter [if n0_road_porter]
-> third_plain

== third_porter
Traveller: That's the third pilgrim this month. And every one of them bound for your abbey, to see the saint.
-> rumour

== third_plain
Traveller: That's the third pilgrim this month. The carter says you're for the abbey in the lane.
Traveller: That's where they were all bound. To see the saint.
-> rumour

== rumour
* What do people say it is? -> demon
* I'll see for myself what's there. -> see

== demon
Traveller: A demon. A thing with horns that walks the wall when the bells are done.
Traveller: I don't say it's true. I say I'd not sleep in there for the King's own purse.
-> end

== see
Traveller: You will, brother. That's what worries me.
-> end

== again
Traveller: Nearly at the wall. Keep your hood up, brother.
-> end

== leave
Traveller: Suit yourself. You'll see soon enough.
"
